e)","7130","mrgid","",""]]},"P8G4J":{"d":[["Distribution. Botswana, Gabon, Madagascar, South Africa.","","text","",""]]},"PFTC":{"d":[["","50","tdwg","native",""],["Australia","","text","native",""]]},"PGDLF":{"d":[["","TW","iso","native",""]]},"PGWF9":{"d":[["","CO","iso","native",""]]},"Q3ZX7":{"d":[["Distribution: Bangladesh, Cambodia, Indonesia, Malaysia, Laos, Thailand and Vietnam. In Myanmar, recorded in Lampi Marine National Park (Bisi et al. 2019) and possibly distributed in Tanintharyi Region.","","text","",""]]},"QMS8D":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"QS7R":{"d":[["Mexico (Oaxaca)","","text","",""]]},"R6SXZ":{"d":[["Norway","NO","iso","",""],["Norway","NO","iso","",""]]},"RRMPL":{"d":[["ZA, Eastern Cape","","text","native",""]]},"RRQHP":{"d":[["Distribution and bionomic. The species is known only from the type-locality, Northern Thailand, Prov. Lampang. The adults have been breaded from larvae collected in beginning of June in valley sparse forest along river. The larvae feed on Cyclea peltata, Menispermaceae. Adults emerged 17 and 18 of June. Note. The species was illustrated and referred by Kononenko and Pinratana (2013) as “ Plusiodonta sp. unidentified, cf. casta Buller, 1878 ”.","","text","",""]]},"RST4":{"d":[["Bangladesh","","text","native",""],["Borneo","","text","native",""],["India","","text","native",""],["Indonesia","","text","native",""],["Laos","","text","native",""],["Malaysia","","text","native",""],["Myanmar","","text","native",""],["Philippines","","text","native",""],["Vietnam","","text","native",""]]},"RT34":{"d":[["","BZC","tdwg","",""]]},"RV39Y":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"RWL8":{"d":[["Brazil","","text","",""]]},"S2JSK":{"d":[["DISTRIBUTION. Laos, northern Thailand, Cambodia.","","text","",""]]},"S8DMQ":{"d":[["Norway","NO","iso","",""],["Norway","NO","iso","",""]]},"SPJ9G":{"d":[["Japan Sea/East Sea","4307","mrgid","native",""]]},"SRW8Y":{"d":[["Distribution and ecology. This taxon was surveyed in the lower reaches of Lao river (North Calabria), at elevations of 130 - 350 m, where it grows on rocky metamorphic outcrops (Fig. 10). It likes humid and shady stands covered by a dense moss carpet, associated mainly to Adiantum capillus-veneris. As for the other subspecies previously examined, it is linked to hygrophilous communities of the Adiantetea capilli-veneris too. From a phytogeographical point of view, it should be noted that this taxon is the only Solenopsis with a perennial habit, localized in a continental territory since all the others occur exclusively in big Mediterranean islands (Crespo et al. 1998).","","text","",""]]},"SWHGT":{"d":[["Nepal; Bhutan; India (Arunachal Pradesh, Assam, Meghalaya, Sikkim); Bangladesh; Myanmar; Thailand; Laos; Vietnam","","text","",""]]},"T3NX":{"d":[["India (Tamil Nadu)","","text","",""]]},"TBPG":{"d":[["Madagascar","","text","native",""]]},"TCSJ9":{"d":[["DISTRIBUTION: Palawan (Philippine Isis.).","","text","",""]]},"TMYS":{"d":[["Mozambique","","text","native",""]]},"TMZ2":{"d":[["MADAGASCAR","","text","native",""]]},"TP97Y":{"d":[["Distribution. South Africa (Turton 1932).","","text","",""]]},"V29JB":{"d":[["","GRC","tdwg","",""]]},"V3XHD":{"d":[["Southern Asia","","text","",""]]},"V4YCG":{"d":[["Henan","48058","mrgid","",""]]},"V58CG":{"d":[["TWN","TW","iso","",""]]},"V5GDW":{"d":[["Utah","25127","mrgid","",""]]},"V6DGV":{"d":[["Africa","","text","",""],["Europe & Northern Asia (excluding China)","","text","",""]]},"VBNNY":{"d":[["Hebei","48048","mrgid","",""]]},"VCH93":{"d":[["Locality and horizon The fossil remains of Ligabuesaurus come from the Cerro de los Leones locality, a hill located ~ 10 km to the southwest of Picún Leufú city, southern Neuquén Province, Patagonia, Argentina (Fig. 1 A, B). The fluvial deposits outcropping in this area were referred to the lower section of the Cullin Grande Member (Martinelli et al., 2007), the upper member of the Lohan Cura Formation (Bajada del Agrio Group, Lower Cretaceous, Albian). The type quarry (no. 4) was opened in the fossiliferous level no. 2 (sensu Martinelli et al., 2007) in the southern flank of the Cerro de los Leones (Fig. 1 C) and 40 m to the east of quarry no. 3, where part of the referred specimen was found (Supporting Information, Table S 1). The sauropod remains were found in laminate mudstones with interbedded fine- to very fine-grained sandstones. These fluvial deposits were dated as Albian and are considered to have been formed in a distal floodplain in semi-arid climatic conditions (Martinelli et al., 2007).","","text","",""]]},"VCKR7":{"d":[["Distribution. Known only from Mexico (Mexico and Puebla States).","","text","",""]]},"W9YD":{"d":[["Australia","","text","native",""]]},"XJ56":{"d":[["CHI-NM","CHI-NM","tdwg","",""]]},"YG85":{"d":[["Antarctica","8588","mrgid","",""]]}}